It will select one by one each element and it will put it in the right place.It will loop through all the elements of an array and will try to find out the minimum element of the array,so it will go to each element one by one and it will select the minimum element.After selection,it will move the element on first index.Here n-1 iterations will be happened

See image of How selection sort works.png

Solution:
let arr=[9,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8];
  let n=arr.length;
for (let i=0;i<n-1;i++){
  let min=i
   for (let j=i+1;j<n;j++){
     if (arr[j]<arr[min]){
     
       min=j
   }}
 let temp=arr[i]
     arr[i]=arr[min]
     arr[min]=temp
}
console.log(arr)


